# The `+` menu's New ▸ child: the pointer opens it on row 0 (un-highlighted,
# as Rust's child starts), two downs land on the THIRD row and Enter runs it —
# the HTTP request opens. The first arrow used to only light the cursor, so
# every later key was one row above where the screen said it was, `→`
# curated the row above and Enter pinned instead of creating (walkthrough 2.2).
click 33 1
expect screen contains "Create…"
hover 36 3
expect screen contains "Scratch buffer"
key down
key down
key enter
expect screen lacks "Create…"
expect screen contains "new request"
